      LAW — archetype budget values are EVIDENCE-BOUND IN BOTH DIRECTIONS.
      Raise a value only on observed failure at the current value (OOM record,
      CFS-throttle evidence, crashloop trace). Lower a value only with evidence
      that the ORIGINAL bump's cause is cured — never on the assumption that a
      co-landed fix (probe, template change) was the whole cause. The 2026-07-16
      down-realignment of recycled-laptop to 1000m rested on a probe-only
      assumption; it resurfaced 2026-08-03 as 100% CFS throttle and 2026-08-08
      as SILENT gossip-dark (kitsune2 skips initiation debug-only on a starved,
      never-populated peer store — the peer looks Ready while outside the DHT).
      Record the evidence as a $-comment on the changed value IN THE SAME EDIT.
      Twin guard at the runtime seam: elohim/elohim-storage/src/.epr-meta
      (rule config-knobs-honor-the-floor).
